    "multicolumn_3iwpyD": {
      "type": "multicolumn",
      "blocks": {
        "column_nGRh6z": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "<strong>Negative Ions</strong>",
            "text": "<p>When properly heated, Himalayan salt lamps emit negative ions up to 4 feet around the surface area of the lamp.<br/>The negative ions neutralize positive ions in the air such as:</p><ul><li>Allergens</li><li>EMFS</li><li>Virus & Bacteria</li><li>Odors</li><li>Mold & Mildew</li></ul>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_CUFKnU": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "<strong>How They Work</strong>",
            "text": "<p>Salt naturally attracts moisture from the air.<br/>When the salt is warm, the moisture evaporates.<br/><br/>This action causes negative ions to be released into the air.</p><p><br/>Your salt lamp must have an incandescent light bulb to create the necessary heat.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_9dk7L3": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "<strong>A Calming Effect</strong>",
            "text": "<p>Negative ions are why the air is so amazing after a thunderstorm and why we feel calm and relaxed at the beach.</p><p><strong>Best Places for a Salt Lamp are:</strong></p><ul><li>Next to a computer</li><li>Where you watch TV</li><li>Nightstand</li><li>By a favorite chair</li><li>Kitchen table</li><li>Child’s room</li><li>Pet area</li></ul>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": "shopify://pages/benefits-of-himalayan-salt-lamps"
          }
        }
      },
